  "body": "When using the `setRxBoostedGainMode` parameter, I noticed that the gain value was not being configured or applied correctly. \nIt appears there might be a minor logical issue—or is there perhaps another design consideration at play?\n\n\n`src\\modules\\LR2021\\LR2021_config.cpp`\n\n```\nint16_t LR2021::setRxBoostedGainMode(uint8_t level) {\n  int16_t state = this->setRxPath(this->highFreq ? RADIOLIB_LR2021_RX_PATH_HF : RADIOLIB_LR2021_RX_PATH_LF, this->highFreq ? this->gainModeHf : this->gainModeLf);\n  RADIOLIB_ASSERT(state);\n  if(this->highFreq) {\n    this->gainModeHf = level;\n  } else {\n    this->gainModeLf = level;\n  }\n  return(state);\n}\n```\nHere, the configuration command is invoked first, utilizing the default values ​​defined within the class rather than the passed-in parameter values; the passed-in parameter values ​​will only be utilized during the subsequent invocation.\n\nThis looks more normal.\n```\nint16_t LR2021::setRxBoostedGainMode(uint8_t level) {\n  if(this->highFreq) {\n    this->gainModeHf = level;\n  } else {\n    this->gainModeLf = level;\n  }\n  int16_t state = this->setRxPath(this->highFreq ? RADIOLIB_LR2021_RX_PATH_HF : RADIOLIB_LR2021_RX_PATH_LF, this->highFreq ? this->gainModeHf : this->gainModeLf);\n  RADIOLIB_ASSERT(state);\n  return(state);\n}\n```",
